  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nMainly dry conditions are expected to continue through the remainder \nof the week and beginning of the weekend. High pressure over the \nOhio Valley and Lower Great Lakes will exit to the east as a cold \nfront swings southeast across the region Wednesday evening. Most of \nthe forecast area will remain dry with the frontal passage outside \nof low-end PoPs in lake enhanced rain showers across Northwest \nPennsylvania Wednesday night. Another area of high pressure \nbuilds overhead behind the cold front which will continue the \nprolonged dry conditions through Saturday night. \n\nHigh temperature through the period will generally remain in the \nupper 60s to lower 70s. Slightly warmer highs possible Wednesday and \nSaturday in the mid 70s as a warm front will lift across the \nregion both days.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nBy Sunday, a disturbance originating from the \nGulf will move north towards the Tennessee and Ohio Valleys \nbringing increased tropical moisture to the region. If the \nforecasted track persists, widespread rainfall is expected \nSunday into Monday. Will continue to monitor forecast trends \nwith this disturbance in the coming days.",
